# Anime-clip teaching format

Reference look: Instagram Reels dual-pane explainers (e.g. genoa_nopi_japanese — white JP+romaji card over yellow EN). **JD’s version is not repeat-and-translate** — he **explains the grammar / nuance** while the anime line is on screen.

## Layout (1080×1920)

1. **Top half** — JD face cam (talking to camera). One shot of him, not a second video of the board.
2. **Bottom half** — the **anime clip** (or source scene) that has the line.
3. **Center stack** (over the seam between face and anime):
   - **White rounded card** — Japanese line on top, **romaji under it** (same card).
   - **Yellow card** directly under — English meaning (natural / punchy, can be rough).

Do **not** use the old board-over-face lesson stack for anime teaches. Do **not** use face-only zoom with no anime pane for this format.

## What goes on screen vs what he says

| On screen | In his mouth / audio |
|-----------|----------------------|
| The line (JP + romaji) | He **explains** it — grammar, nuance, who says it, why that form, trap vs normal, etc. |
| EN on the yellow card | Translation is support; **not** the whole video. Don’t make a “say it / here’s English” loop. |

She (reference) mostly repeats the line and translates. **We don’t.** Hook can still be the line or the vibe; the meat is the explain.

## Caption / card rules

- White card: JP then romaji. Keep readable; don’t crowd.
- Yellow card: EN only.
- Spoken captions (if burned later) still follow oneblock punctuation rules (no `,` `.` `;` `:` `。` in burned spoken text). The JP/romaji/EN **cards** can use normal punctuation for the line itself when matching the reference look.
- CTA / end card: same locked line as other Reels when shipping a finished post (`Book a trial lesson` → link in bio on IG).

## When building or prompting

- Call this format **anime dual-pane** (face top / anime bottom + white JP·romaji + yellow EN).
- CapCut / ffmpeg / pipeline prompts must name that stack explicitly.
- If he only drops an anime clip path with no face take yet, still plan the dual-pane and note face cam is required for the final.

## Related

- Lesson-OBS Shorts (whiteboard lessons): different format — face zoom or lesson crop; hunt warning / analogy / wrong-then-right. See `shorts-reel-post-workflow.mdc`.
- This rule wins for **anime / clip-line teaching** posts.
